WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:04.900
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.200
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.500
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演过《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:08.740
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.560
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:19.540
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:20.700
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:26.230
Hi.
嗨。

9
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:34.270
We're recording in the afternoon, so I was wondering what you might say, because it's not morning, and you always say good morning.
我们在下午录音，所以我很好奇你会怎么打招呼，因为现在不是早上，而你总是说早上好。

10
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:35.070
It's true.
确实。

11
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:35.710
It's true.
确实。

12
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:37.710
This is a very rare occasion for us.
这对我们来说是非常罕见的情况。

13
00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:38.370
It is.
没错。

14
00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:41.890
I actually want to start off by saying thank you.
其实我想先说声谢谢。

15
00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:49.950
And I might get emotional right at the top, but I had a medical emergency with my mom, and I flew back home to Texas.
刚开始我可能就会情绪激动，但我妈妈突发了医疗紧急状况，我飞回了德克萨斯州的家中。

16
00:00:50.330 --> 00:01:02.870
And I just want you guys out there to know that Jenna and Cassie and Sam and everyone at Office Ladies Pod and Earwolf just let me – I just left.
我只想让大家知道，珍娜、卡西、萨姆，还有《办公室》女士播客和Earwolf的所有人，他们让我——我当时直接就走了。

17
00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.410
I just dropped everything and left.
我放下一切就走了。

18
00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:04.930
You did.
你确实这么做了。

19
00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:05.790
And there was –
当时——

20
00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:06.570
And we were fine.
我们没问题的。

21
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:07.650
And there were no questions.
而且没有任何疑问。

22
00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.690
You guys were just like, get home to your mom.
你们当时就说，快回家陪你妈妈吧。

23
00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:16.990
And it just meant so much to me to have that support that I could do that, and I could go there and be with her.
能得到这样的支持，让我可以去陪在她身边，这对我意义重大。

24
00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.090
And everything's okay now.
现在一切都好了。

25
00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.770
It was a scary few days.
那几天真的很吓人。

26
00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:24.390
But I'm just so thankful for you, Jenna.
但我真的很感激你，珍娜。

27
00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:29.470
And I'm so thankful that we get to do this podcast because family comes firSt.
我也很感激我们能一起做这个播客，因为家庭永远是第一位的。

28
00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:36.830
Well, Angela, I think I speak for everyone when I say that it was our pleasure to make that space for you,
安吉拉，我想我代表大家说，能为你腾出时间是我们的荣幸，

29
00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:42.230
and we're so glad that you were able to be there with her because family does come firSt.
我们很高兴你能陪在她身边，因为家庭确实是第一位的。

30
00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:48.010
And we're recording in the afternoon so I could have an extended time with her.
我们选在下午录音，这样我就能多陪她一会儿了。

31
00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:48.390
Yeah.
没错。

32
00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.730
And what are we talking about?
那我们今天要聊什么呢？

33
00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:52.890
Well, today –
嗯，今天——

34
00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.490
I'm so out of it.
我状态不太好。

35
00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:56.890
We are talking about Last Day in Florida.
我们要聊的是《佛罗里达的最后一天》。

36
00:01:57.070 --> 00:01:57.650
Oh, right.
哦，对。

37
00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:58.070
Yes.
是的。

38
00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:04.070
It is Season 8, Episode 18, written by Robert Padnick and directed by Matt Sohn.
这是第八季第十八集，由罗伯特·帕德尼克编剧，马特·索恩执导。

39
00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.430
And here's your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

40
00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:16.070
As their time in Florida comes to a close, Jim tries to warn Dwight about Robert California's secret plan to sandbag the Saber store and fire him.
随着在佛罗里达的时间即将结束，吉姆试图警告德怀特，罗伯特·加州有一个秘密计划，要让赛博商店项目失败并解雇他。

41
00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:25.150
Meanwhile, Daryl and Toby compete to sell Girl Scout cookies, and Erin decides to stay in Florida and be Irene's live-in helper.
与此同时，达里尔和托比竞争销售女童子军饼干，而艾琳决定留在佛罗里达，做艾琳的住家帮手。

42
00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:28.610
I love almost every single thing Irene has to say.
我喜欢艾琳说的几乎每一句话。

43
00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:29.850
She's wonderful.
她太棒了。

44
00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:30.850
She's so great.
她真的很棒。

45
00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.090
Her deliveries are great.
她的台词表达方式太赞了。

46
00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.550
I wanted Irene to come back to Dunder Mifflin.
我真希望艾琳能回到邓德·米夫林。

47
00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.330
That would be perfect.
那简直太完美了。

48
00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:44.030
But this was an episode that had three very distinct storylines in three different locations.
但这一集有三条非常清晰的故事线，发生在三个不同的地点。

49
00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:48.250
So we had to kind of keep toggling back and forth between all these different places.
所以我们得在这些不同的地方之间来回切换。

50
00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:52.430
Fast fact number one, James Spader, a.k.a.
冷知识第一条，詹姆斯·斯派德，也就是

51
00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:53.970
Robert California, is back.
罗伯特·加利福尼亚回来了。

52
00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:54.770
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

53
00:02:55.150 --> 00:03:02.390
You guys might remember that we shared early on when James Spader was contemplating whether or not he wanted to join our show,
大家可能还记得，在詹姆斯·斯派德考虑是否要加入我们的剧组之初，我们就分享过，

54
00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:05.390
that he had this opportunity to shoot the movie Lincoln.
他当时有机会去拍电影《林肯》。

55
00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.470
And he said, I will come.
他说，我会来的。

56
00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:11.690
I will do a full season of your show, but you must give me time off to go do this movie Lincoln.
我会拍满你们的一整季，但你们必须给我时间去拍这部《林肯》。

57
00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:12.310
Right.
没错。

58
00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:13.670
That's where he was.
他当时就是这么个情况。

59
00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:14.730
That's where he's been.
他一直都在忙那个。

60
00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.470
Why we haven't seen him in a while.
这就是为什么我们有一阵子没见到他了。

61
00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.350
And so Lincoln wrapped.
后来《林肯》杀青了。

62
00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:21.150
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

63
00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:22.770
And now here we are.
现在我们就在这儿了。

64
00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:26.130
And we also shot this episode in January 2012.
我们也是在2012年1月拍摄的这一集。

65
00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:28.230
It was right after our holiday break.
就在我们假期结束之后。

66
00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:30.510
Everyone was back.
大家都回来了。

67
00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:35.330
Everyone was, I guess, rested and excited to get back to work.
我想大家应该都休息好了，也对重返工作岗位感到兴奋。

68
00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:41.310
So if you think maybe we have a little more pep in our step in this episode, it's because we'd all come back from our holiday break.
所以如果你觉得我们在这一集里看起来更有活力，那是因为我们刚度完假回来。

69
00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:42.230
We were rested.
我们休息得很充分。

70
00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:42.950
Right.
没错。

71
00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:48.950
All right, fast fact number two, guess what else was happening at this time?
好了，第二个小知识，猜猜当时还发生了什么？

72
00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.630
Well, I know because I went in my digital clutter.
嗯，我知道，因为我翻了翻我的数字杂物。

73
00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:52.330
Yes.
是的。

74
00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:59.010
You shared the other week that Greg Daniels congratulated us on our SAG Award nomination.
你前几周提到过，格雷格·丹尼尔斯祝贺我们获得了演员工会奖提名。

75
00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:01.230
And now here it was time to go.
现在正是要去参加颁奖礼的时候了。

76
00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:01.670
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

77
00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:04.870
This was our fifth time attending the SAG Awards.
这是我们第五次参加演员工会奖。

78
00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:08.370
We had been nominated as a cast every year since 2007.
自2007年以来，我们每年都以剧组名义获得提名。

79
00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:15.190
And this one was a particularly memorable one for me because I was four months postpartum.
这一次对我来说特别难忘，因为我当时刚产后四个月。

80
00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:18.490
And I was really nervous about getting on a red carpet.
我真的很紧张，担心走红毯的事。

81
00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:19.890
I hadn't done that yet.
我还没经历过那种场合。

82
00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:20.430
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

83
00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:23.670
Hadn't had to stand in front of a bank of photographers.
还没试过站在一排摄影师面前。

84
00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:24.430
Yeah.
是啊。

85
00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.530
In my postpartum-ness.
带着我那产后的身体。

86
00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:30.050
And remember I told you about the coat closet where they let me pump?
还记得我跟你说过那个让我挤奶的衣帽间吗？

87
00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:34.950
And I brought my pump with me and I pumped at the SAG Awards.
我带上了吸奶器，在演员工会奖现场挤了奶。

88
00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:35.750
Whoop, whoop!
哇哦，太棒了！

89
00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:40.650
I remember walking down the red carpet and they asked me, like, who I was wearing.
我记得走在红毯上时，他们问我穿的是什么品牌的衣服。

90
00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:43.450
So I did a little bit that my handbag was my pump.
所以我开玩笑说我的手提包就是我的吸奶器。

91
00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:48.910
If you see pictures of me from this red carpet, you can tell I need to pump.
如果你看我当时在红毯上的照片，就能看出我需要去挤奶了。

92
00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:52.270
I am falling out of my dress.
我都要从礼服里溢出来了。

93
00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:54.010
Yes, a little bit.
是的，确实有点。

94
00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:58.610
I thought you looked so radiant and beautiful and I loved the color of your dress.
我觉得你当时看起来容光焕发，非常漂亮，而且我很喜欢你那件礼服的颜色。

95
00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.010
Oh, thank you, lady.
噢，谢谢你，亲爱的。

96
00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:01.670
I was so nervous.
我当时紧张极了。

97
00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:09.190
And this designer, Max Azria Atelier, offered to make me a custom gown.
这位设计师，Max Azria Atelier，主动提出要为我定制一件礼服。

98
00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:12.410
Like, designed it for my postpartum body.
就是专门为我产后的身材设计的。

99
00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:17.370
Because I don't know if people know, but when you borrow a dress, they have something called sample sizes.
因为我不知道大家知不知道，当你借礼服时，他们有所谓的样衣尺码。

100
00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:18.110
Yeah.
是啊。

101
00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:19.970
Sample sizes are very, very small.
样衣的尺码非常、非常小。

102
00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:24.470
And oftentimes, even before I had had a baby, I couldn't fit into sample sizes.
而且很多时候，甚至在我生孩子之前，我就穿不进样衣。

103
00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.970
Also, sample sizes don't fit short people.
另外，样衣也不适合个子矮的人。

104
00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:27.530
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

105
00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:28.310
So there's that.
所以就是这样。

106
00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:35.050
But sometimes they would be able to, like, take out the seams a little bit on the sample sizes and I could get myself into one.
但有时候他们能把样衣的接缝稍微放开一点，我才能勉强穿进去。

107
00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:39.670
But I had a hard time borrowing a dress and this designer made me one from scratch.
但我很难借到礼服，于是这位设计师为我量身定做了一件。

108
00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:42.350
And, oh, my gosh, I remember getting there.
天哪，我记得当时抵达现场的情景。

109
00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.430
I remember running into John and Emily.
我记得遇到了约翰和艾米丽。

110
00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.570
I remember running into you, running into Brian.
我记得遇到了你，还有布莱恩。

111
00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.270
You all were so kind to me.
你们对我真的太好了。

112
00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:53.230
And you just, like, held me up and gave me all this confidence.
你们就像是支撑着我，给了我满满的自信。

113
00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:54.590
It was absolutely amazing.
那感觉真是太棒了。

114
00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.050
And, lady, I remember what you wore to this.
而且，亲爱的，我还记得你当时穿了什么。

115
00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:57.710
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

116
00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:59.170
I wore a vintage dress.
我穿了一件复古礼服。

117
00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:02.770
It looked like old Hollywood Grecian.
看起来像是老好莱坞的希腊风格。

118
00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:03.810
It was light blue.
是浅蓝色的。

119
00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:04.250
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

120
00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:08.590
The way you did your hair was kind of like this nod to old Hollywood, I felt like.
我觉得你当时的发型设计，就像是在向老好莱坞致敬。

121
00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:10.910
It was so gorgeous.
真是太美了。

122
00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:11.770
It was a great look.
那身造型很赞。

123
00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:12.410
Thanks.
谢谢。

124
00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:13.430
It was true vintage.
那是真正的复古款。

125
00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:15.090
I'd never done that before.
我以前从没尝试过那种风格。

126
00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:17.330
And I did, like, the soft waves.
我做了那种柔和的波浪卷发。

127
00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:19.790
I was going really hard for, like, LA Confidential.
我当时真的很想打造出《洛城机密》那种感觉。

128
00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:20.310
Yes.
没错。

129
00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:20.870
Yes.
是的。

130
00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.830
That's kind of what it seemed like.
看起来确实是那样。

131
00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:25.050
Well, we had a great night that night.
那天晚上我们过得很愉快。

132
00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:26.570
We had so much fun.
我们玩得太开心了。

133
00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:27.370
So much fun.
真的太开心了。

134
00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:28.510
I sat next to BJ.
我坐在BJ旁边。

135
00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:30.910
And I was really hungry.
我当时真的很饿。

136
00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:33.190
And, you know, there's not a ton of food.
你知道的，那里没多少吃的。

137
00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:35.810
And BJ gave me all of his breadsticks.
BJ把他所有的面包棒都给了我。

138
00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:37.430
And I'll never forget it.
我永远都不会忘记这件事。

139
00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:38.930
Why do I think I remember this?
为什么我觉得我记得这个？

140
00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:40.910
And then guess what else I did?
然后你猜我还做了什么？

141
00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:45.030
I will always get my words just a little bit off, you know?
我总是会把词说错一点点，你知道吧？

142
00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:46.310
We know.
我们知道。

143
00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:47.210
And my mom.
还有我妈。

144
00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.070
We've been there with you.
我们都陪你经历过这些。

145
00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.430
My mom does this.
我妈也会这样。

146
00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.490
Like, my mom will say, have you seen Office?
比如，我妈会问，你看过《办公室》吗？

147
00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:53.270
It's not The Office, right?
不是叫《办公室风云》，对吧？

148
00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:55.990
And basically, I'm turning into my mom in this way.
基本上，我在这一点上正变得越来越像我妈。

149
00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:59.830
So at that time, the president of NBC was Bob Greenblatt.
当时，NBC的总裁是鲍勃·格林布拉特。

150
00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:02.730
And he had been a big champion of this new show.
他一直是这部新剧的坚定支持者。

151
00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:03.330
Yes.
是的。

152
00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:03.830
Yeah, no, no.
对，不，不是。

153
00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:04.590
Don't say the name.
别说那个名字。

154
00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:05.290
Don't say the name.
别说那个名字。

155
00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:05.510
Okay.
好吧。

156
00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:07.530
Debra Messing was the lead.
黛博拉·梅辛是主演。

157
00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:08.770
It was about Broadway.
那是关于百老汇的。

158
00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:12.290
I had watched the pilot episode, and I liked it.
我看了试播集，我很喜欢。

159
00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:15.610
And I said to him, hey, I love Smashed.
我就对他说，嘿，我超爱《Smashed》。

160
00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:18.830
And he said, thanks.
他说，谢谢。

161
00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:19.950
It's Smash.
那是《Smash》。

162
00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:22.130
And I was like, uh-huh.
我当时就，呃，嗯。

163
00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:26.390
Smashed is like a whole other show.
《Smashed》是完全另外一部剧。

164
00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:30.050
It's about just a bunch of drunken 20-year-olds.
那讲的是一群喝得烂醉的二十岁年轻人。

165
00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:33.050
Is any wonder I haven't been on another NBC show?
难怪我再也没上过NBC的节目了，对吧？

166
00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:35.570
The president was like, get rid of that idiot.
总裁当时说，把那个白痴弄走。

167
00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:40.370
And then the other thing I remember from this night is, you know, we were at these really
那天晚上我记得的另一件事是，我们当时坐在那些非常

168
00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:41.070
long tables.
长的桌子旁。

169
00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:44.790
And BJ and I were at one end, sort of towards the stage.
BJ和我坐在桌子的一端，离舞台比较近。

170
00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:48.690
And way at the other end, by this walkway, is where John was sitting.
而在另一端，靠近过道的地方，是约翰坐的位置。

171
00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:54.970
And we had these oversized bottles of wine that they set on the table.
桌上放着他们准备的超大瓶红酒。

172
00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:55.530
Yeah.
对。

173
00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:57.290
You know, like the big, big bottles.
你知道，就是那种特别特别大的瓶子。

174
00:07:57.650 --> 00:08:00.690
They, like, went up to, like, your thigh if you set them on the ground.
如果放在地上，大概能到你的大腿那么高。

175
00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:00.990
Yeah.
对。

176
00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:03.850
They were kind of, like, decorative, but yet you could open them and drink them.
它们看起来像是装饰品，但其实是可以打开喝的。

177
00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:07.630
So John, his side of the table hadn't opened theirs yet.
约翰那一侧的桌子还没开他们的那瓶。

178
00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:11.410
And Matt Damon walked by and said hi to John and Emily.
马特·达蒙走过来，跟约翰和艾米丽打了招呼。

179
00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:12.730
And they were chatting.
他们聊了一会儿。

180
00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:15.050
And then he turned to all of us.
然后他转向我们所有人。

181
00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:17.170
And he goes, hey, are you not drinking this wine?
他说，嘿，你们不喝这瓶酒吗？

182
00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:18.150
And we're like, oh.
我们说，噢。

183
00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:19.350
And he goes, can I take it?
他说，我可以拿走吗？

184
00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:20.210
And we're like, sure.
我们说，当然可以。

185
00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.710
So Matt Damon took our giant oversized bottle of wine.
于是马特·达蒙拿走了我们那瓶超大的红酒。

186
00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:27.130
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

187
00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:27.830
That's amazing.
太绝了。

188
00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:32.030
Well, I do know that I didn't stay out too late after this one.
嗯，我知道在那之后我没在外面待太晚。

189
00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:34.910
