我发现自己登上了所有能上的“最差着装榜”。

196
00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:56.750
And this was.
而且这是。

197
00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:57.390
Seriously?
真的吗？

198
00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:58.110
Yes.
是的。

199
00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:03.350
This was the year that the woman wrote her, like, worst dress liSt.
那一年，那个女人写了她的“最差着装榜”。

200
00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:07.950
And she said that she knew that I only gave birth about four months ago.
她说她知道我才刚生完孩子四个月左右。

201
00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:10.990
But, like, seriously, I couldn't look better than I did.
但说真的，我当时的状态好得不能再好了。

202
00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:12.410
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

203
00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:13.510
So tacky.
太俗气了。

204
00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:15.410
So tacky.
太俗气了。

205
00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:15.590
Tacky.
俗气。

206
00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:19.230
I don't think we should have worst dress lists.
我觉得我们不该搞什么最差着装榜。

207
00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:19.690
Period.
没商量。

208
00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:23.530
Why are we commenting negatively on people's appearance?
我们为什么要对别人的外表进行负面评价呢？

209
00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:25.410
We are adults now, right?
我们现在都是成年人了，对吧？

210
00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:25.770
Yeah.
是啊。

211
00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:28.610
Like, have we not learned anything?
我们难道还没学到什么吗？

212
00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:29.530
I know.
我知道。

213
00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:31.910
Get rid of worst dressed lists.
取消最差着装榜吧。

214
00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:32.850
Nobody cares.
没人会在意那个。

215
00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:33.690
No.
没错。

216
00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:34.450
They suck.
那太烂了。

217
00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:34.730
They suck.
那太烂了。

218
00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:35.530
And they're unnecessary.
而且完全没必要。

219
00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:36.610
And they're tacky.
而且很俗气。

220
00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:37.290
Yeah.
是啊。

221
00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:38.410
Yeah, exactly.
没错，确实。

222
00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:38.870
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

223
00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:41.170
Well, put her on my tacky liSt.
好吧，把她列入我的俗气名单。

224
00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:41.870
Yeah.
好。

225
00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:43.050
I know her name.
我知道她的名字。

226
00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:44.450
Don't think I have forgotten.
别以为我忘了。

227
00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:45.170
I know.
我知道。

228
00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:46.590
I know, Aria Stark.
我知道，艾莉亚·史塔克。

229
00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:49.490
All right.
好吧。

230
00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:52.490
Well, moving on to fast fact number three.
那么，进入第三个快讯。

231
00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:56.310
Have you heard of a blog called Ask a Manager?
你们听说过一个叫“问问经理”的博客吗？

232
00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:58.190
No.
没有。

233
00:09:58.610 --> 00:09:58.990
Okay.
好吧。

234
00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:01.390
It's run by this woman named Allison Green.
它是由一位名叫艾莉森·格林的女士运营的。

235
00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:03.090
She's a manager.
她是一位经理。

236
00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:03.650
Okay.
好的。

237
00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:08.030
And she answers questions, like business questions, business advice questions.
她会回答各种问题，比如职场问题、职场建议类的问题。

238
00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:08.430
Okay.
好的。

239
00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:12.450
About everything from hiring, firing, promoting, managing, everything.
内容涵盖招聘、解雇、晋升、管理等方方面面。

240
00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:18.170
And I thought, you know, last week we answered people's questions on our podcaSt.
我在想，你知道，上周我们在播客里回答了听众的问题。

241
00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:18.910
Yeah, we did.
是啊，我们回答了。

242
00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:19.990
Dear office ladies.
亲爱的办公室女士们。

243
00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:21.050
Dear office ladies.
亲爱的办公室女士们。

244
00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:24.310
I wondered what Allison would think of the advice we gave.
我在想艾莉森会怎么看我们给出的建议。

245
00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:27.550
Did you ask her?
你问她了吗？

246
00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:28.250
I didn't.
我没问。

247
00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:28.890
Can you type it in?
你能打字问问吗？

248
00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:30.470
No, I didn't ask her.
不，我没问她。

