00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:18.810
So Allison said, you don't generally need a dedicated HR person until you hit more like
艾莉森说，通常情况下，员工人数达到50人以上才需要专门的人力资源专员。

260
00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:20.010
50 employees.
50名员工。

261
00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:20.630
Hmm.
嗯。

262
00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:24.290
And a lot of companies don't bring one on until they're closer to 100.
很多公司直到员工接近100人时才会聘请专员。

263
00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:30.810
Allison said, you do need someone to handle things like payroll, benefits, administration.
艾莉森说，你确实需要有人来处理工资单、福利和行政等事务。

264
00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:36.050
But in a small business, that's usually more of a clerk position than someone who would
但在小企业里，这通常更像是一个文员职位，而不是那种会从事更高层级人力资源工作的人，

265
00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:44.310
be doing higher-level HR work, like legal compliance or investigations or management coaching.
比如法律合规、调查或管理指导。

266
00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:49.630
Isn't that interesting that the role of an HR person might be management coaching, which
人力资源专员的角色可能包括管理指导，这一点很有趣，

267
00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:51.630
is why Michael hated Toby so much.
这也是迈克尔那么讨厌托比的原因。

268
00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:53.670
But this was my favorite part.
但这是我最喜欢的部分。

269
00:11:53.790 --> 00:12:00.430
Allison went on to say, but if you're asking about Toby on the office, it was never clear
艾莉森接着说，但如果你问的是《办公室》里的托比，我一直没搞明白他为什么会在那儿。

270
00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:01.650
to me why he was there.
就是这样。

271
00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:02.770
There you go.
你说得对。

272
00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:13.190
So, I mean, add that to also three accountants and also a temp who went to Florida and a receptionist
我的意思是，再加上三名会计，还有个去过佛罗里达的临时工，以及一个去过佛罗里达的前台。

273
00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:14.010
that went to Florida.
去过佛罗里达的前台。

274
00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:17.170
Plus, they hired Ryan back after he pretty much...
而且他们还在瑞安几乎……之后又把他雇了回来。

275
00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.710
After he's embezzled from the company, right?
在他挪用公司公款之后，对吧？

276
00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:20.030
Embezzled from the company.
挪用公司公款。

277
00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:23.590
So someone in hiring isn't making super great choices.
所以招聘部门的人选人眼光真不怎么样。

278
00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:28.970
Well, James, maybe you can write to Allison next and ask her if a mid-sized paper company
好吧，詹姆斯，也许下次你可以写信给艾莉森，问问她一家有20名员工的中型造纸公司是否需要三名会计。

279
00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:31.210
with 20 employees needs three accountants.
看看她怎么说。

280
00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:32.370
We'll see what she says.
我们等着瞧。

281
00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:32.730
Yeah.
是啊。

282
00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:35.170
Well, that's all I got, lady.
好吧，我就这些了，女士。

283
00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:36.830
Well, I have a little something to share.
嗯，我也有点东西要分享。

284
00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:40.150
A while back, I was trading emails with Robert Padnick.
前阵子，我和罗伯特·帕德尼克互通了邮件。

285
00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:42.030
And as you know, he wrote this episode.
如你们所知，这一集是他写的。

286
00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:44.010
And I asked him about it.
我问了他关于这一集的事。

287
00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:49.030
And he said it was a really challenging point in the season because there were so many characters
他说这是这一季中非常有挑战性的一点，因为有太多的角色和情节需要兼顾，

288
00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:53.270
