00:52:29.330 --> 00:52:31.350
Well, we also had a fan catch from Aiden W.
另外，我们还收到了一位来自俄勒冈州波特兰市的粉丝艾登·W的发现，他说，

1307
00:52:31.470 --> 00:52:33.010
in Portland, Oregon, who said,
天哪。

1308
00:52:33.330 --> 00:52:34.030
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1309
00:52:34.190 --> 00:52:37.590
Dwight cracks a joke about Jim's hair and everyone laughs.
德怀特开了个关于吉姆发型的玩笑，大家都笑了。

1310
00:52:37.790 --> 00:52:41.790
And then Gabe tries to high-five Kathy and she totally rejects it.
然后盖博想和凯西击掌，结果被她彻底无视了。

1311
00:52:41.870 --> 00:52:43.890
It was a hilarious background choice.
这是一个非常搞笑的背景细节。

1312
00:52:44.610 --> 00:52:47.990
So, I checked the script because I saw this little beat.
于是我查了剧本，因为我注意到了这个小插曲。

1313
00:52:48.230 --> 00:52:49.630
It was not scripted.
这不是剧本里写的。

1314
00:52:50.090 --> 00:52:52.090
This is what was scripted.
剧本里写的是这样的。

1315
00:52:53.070 --> 00:52:54.250
Dwight says, quote,
德怀特说，引用如下：

1316
00:52:54.490 --> 00:52:55.070
What is it?
怎么了？

1317
00:52:55.150 --> 00:52:57.390
Your hairstylist ran out of messy spray?
你的发型师没乱发喷雾了吗？

1318
00:52:58.070 --> 00:53:00.310
People laugh obsequitously.
人们谄媚地笑了。

1319
00:53:02.350 --> 00:53:02.830
Obsequitously.
谄媚地。

1320
00:53:03.790 --> 00:53:05.630
It says that over and over again.
剧本里反复出现这个词。

1321
00:53:05.870 --> 00:53:12.310
Every time Dwight or Packer give an insult, the script says people laugh obsequitously.
每次德怀特或帕克侮辱别人时，剧本都写着人们谄媚地笑了。

1322
00:53:13.050 --> 00:53:13.530
Obsequitously.
谄媚地。

1323
00:53:13.830 --> 00:53:14.850
How do you say it?
这个词怎么读？

1324
00:53:14.970 --> 00:53:15.870
What does this mean?
这是什么意思？

1325
00:53:15.970 --> 00:53:16.230
I don't know.
我不知道。

1326
00:53:16.310 --> 00:53:17.150
I'd have to read it.
我得读一下。

1327
00:53:18.170 --> 00:53:18.650
Obsequitously.
谄媚地。

1328
00:53:19.630 --> 00:53:20.110
Obsequitously.
谄媚地。

1329
00:53:20.410 --> 00:53:20.630
Yeah.
是啊。

1330
00:53:21.030 --> 00:53:21.510
Obsequitously.
谄媚地。

1331
00:53:21.510 --> 00:53:22.790
Do you know what that means?
你知道那是什么意思吗？

1332
00:53:24.170 --> 00:53:24.710
No.
不知道。

1333
00:53:25.330 --> 00:53:28.870
I mean, Robert Papnick loves obsequitously.
我是说，罗伯特·帕普尼克很喜欢用“谄媚地”这个词。

1334
00:53:29.130 --> 00:53:32.570
It's a very specific adjective.
这是一个非常具体的形容词。

1335
00:53:33.170 --> 00:53:34.510
Are you Googling it?
你在谷歌搜索吗？

1336
00:53:34.590 --> 00:53:34.890
Yeah.
是的。

1337
00:53:35.010 --> 00:53:35.750
I Googled it.
我查了谷歌。

1338
00:53:35.830 --> 00:53:41.270
And it means in an obedient or attentive to an excessive degree.
它的意思是过分顺从或殷勤。

1339
00:53:41.770 --> 00:53:44.550
Oh, so they're laughing at what their boss says is funny.
哦，所以他们笑是因为老板觉得好笑。

1340
00:53:44.730 --> 00:53:45.810
Not anyone else.
而不是因为别人。

1341
00:53:45.930 --> 00:53:47.050
Only the boss is funny.
只有老板才好笑。

1342
00:53:47.050 --> 00:53:47.610
Yes.
没错。

1343
00:53:47.790 --> 00:53:50.250
It's such a specific direction.
这真是个非常具体的指示。

1344
00:53:50.270 --> 00:53:54.470
And I think I know exactly how to laugh at something if I knew what that word meant.
我想如果我知道这个词的意思，我就能准确地知道该怎么笑了。

1345
00:53:54.710 --> 00:53:58.990
But, you know, that you have to laugh because you're pleasing your boss.
但你知道，你必须笑，因为你在讨好你的老板。

1346
00:53:59.050 --> 00:54:00.250
It's the kiss-ass laugh.
这就是马屁精式的笑。

1347
00:54:00.250 --> 00:54:01.990
Yes, the kiss-ass laugh.
没错，马屁精式的笑。

1348
00:54:01.990 --> 00:54:03.990
Robert, you could have just put laugh.
罗伯特，你其实可以直接写“笑”。

1349
00:54:04.270 --> 00:54:04.810
The kiss-ass laugh.
马屁精式的笑。

1350
00:54:04.990 --> 00:54:06.470
Laugh in a kiss-ass way.
用马屁精的方式笑。

1351
00:54:07.130 --> 00:54:10.390
But, no, the proper way to say that is obsequitously.
但不对，那个词的正确说法应该是“卑躬屈膝地”。

1352
00:54:10.950 --> 00:54:14.410
We also had another fan question from Natasha M.
我们还收到了另一位来自英国的粉丝娜塔莎·M的提问。

1353
00:54:14.590 --> 00:54:15.110
in the U.K.
在英国。

1354
00:54:15.450 --> 00:54:16.230
who said,
她说，

1355
00:54:16.430 --> 00:54:18.470
I've been waiting ages to ask this.
我等了好久才问这个问题。

1356
00:54:18.690 --> 00:54:22.590
When Dwight says to Jim, quote, you look like the world's tallest hobbit,
当德怀特对吉姆说，引用一下，“你看起来像世界上最高的霍比特人”时，

1357
00:54:22.810 --> 00:54:25.230
was this a nod to Jim's U.K.
这是在向吉姆的英国版角色提姆致敬吗？

1358
00:54:25.770 --> 00:54:27.730
counterpart, Tim, played by Martin Freeman,
提姆由马丁·弗里曼饰演，

1359
00:54:28.010 --> 00:54:31.070
who also played Bilbo Baggins in The Hobbit?
而他也曾在《霍比特人》中饰演比尔博·巴金斯？

1360
00:54:31.670 --> 00:54:32.090
Oh.
噢。

1361
00:54:33.570 --> 00:54:35.910
Well, Natasha, I don't know.
嗯，娜塔莎，我不知道。

1362
00:54:36.110 --> 00:54:38.310
However, that line was not in the script.
不过，那句台词并不在剧本里。

1363
00:54:38.310 --> 00:54:42.210
I think it was a pitch on the day because the script had Dwight saying,
我觉得那是当天现场提议的，因为剧本里德怀特说的是，

1364
00:54:42.410 --> 00:54:45.570
you should just know that your shadow looks like a sunflower.
“你应该知道你的影子看起来像一朵向日葵”。

1365
00:54:49.410 --> 00:54:52.190
Oh, also, Angela and Natasha from the U.K.
噢，还有，来自英国的安吉拉和娜塔莎

1366
00:54:52.210 --> 00:54:53.330
would like you to know
想让你知道

1367
00:54:53.330 --> 00:54:55.810
that since listening to Office Ladies,
自从听了《办公室女士》之后，

1368
00:54:56.170 --> 00:55:02.410
she has left her previous employer of 22 years to become a trainee train driver.
她辞去了工作了22年的前雇主，去当了一名火车司机实习生。

1369
00:55:02.950 --> 00:55:06.070
And she fully qualified July 7th.
而且她在7月7日顺利拿到了资格证。

1370
00:55:06.790 --> 00:55:09.570
So, Natasha said, I'm not sure when this episode will air,
所以，娜塔莎说，我不确定这集什么时候播出，

1371
00:55:09.710 --> 00:55:13.110
but I will potentially be a qualified train driver by then.
但到那时我可能已经是一名合格的火车司机了。

1372
00:55:13.250 --> 00:55:14.570
And Natasha knows you love trains.
而且娜塔莎知道你喜欢火车。

1373
00:55:14.890 --> 00:55:15.370
I do.
我确实喜欢。

1374
00:55:15.570 --> 00:55:16.650
Way to go, Natasha.
干得好，娜塔莎。

1375
00:55:17.150 --> 00:55:17.550
Congratulations.
恭喜你。

1376
00:55:17.990 --> 00:55:18.330
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1377
00:55:19.090 --> 00:55:20.850
Maybe I'll get to ride on your train someday.
也许有一天我能坐上你开的火车。

1378
00:55:21.490 --> 00:55:23.030
Yeah, when we go to the U.K.
是啊，等我们去英国的时候。

1379
00:55:23.310 --> 00:55:23.550
Yeah.
没错。

1380
00:55:24.230 --> 00:55:25.590
I love taking the train.
我喜欢坐火车。

1381
00:55:26.050 --> 00:55:26.650
Me too.
我也是。

1382
00:55:27.050 --> 00:55:28.670
I just went to another place.
我刚才走神了。

1383
00:55:28.790 --> 00:55:29.350
Did you see me?
你看到我了吗？

1384
00:55:29.450 --> 00:55:31.550
Yeah, you went to your happy train place.
看到了，你去了你的火车快乐老家。

1385
00:55:31.550 --> 00:55:31.810
Okay.
好吧。

1386
00:55:32.410 --> 00:55:35.570
Well, listen, Jim is going to say, I tried.
听着，吉姆要说，我试过了。

1387
00:55:35.750 --> 00:55:38.710
I tried to tell Dwight what was going to happen.
我试着告诉德怀特会发生什么。

1388
00:55:38.730 --> 00:55:40.450
He just made fun of me, basically.
但他基本上只是在取笑我。

1389
00:55:40.450 --> 00:55:41.330
So, I'm out of here.
所以，我走了。

1390
00:55:41.350 --> 00:55:42.250
I have a plane to catch.
我得去赶飞机了。

1391
00:55:42.250 --> 00:55:42.870
He leaves.
他离开了。

1392
00:55:43.590 --> 00:55:43.910
Yes.
是的。

1393
00:55:44.070 --> 00:55:47.110
Add Jim to the list of people who bail and don't lose their job.
把吉姆加进那些临阵脱逃却没丢掉工作的人名单里吧。

1394
00:55:47.330 --> 00:55:47.510
Correct.
没错。

1395
00:55:47.950 --> 00:55:49.790
Well, back at Irene's house,
回到艾琳家，

1396
00:55:50.550 --> 00:55:53.850
Erin has decided to video chat with Andy to let him know
艾琳决定和安迪视频聊天，告诉他

1397
00:55:54.530 --> 00:55:57.270
that she's not going to be working for Dunder Mifflin anymore.
她以后不在邓德·米夫林工作了。

1398
00:55:57.850 --> 00:55:58.290
Yes.
是的。

1399
00:55:58.290 --> 00:56:00.870
Her password is Erin1234.
她的密码是Erin1234。

1400
00:56:02.330 --> 00:56:05.930
Irene knows more about all of this technology than Erin.
艾琳对这些科技的了解比艾琳还要多。

1401
00:56:06.510 --> 00:56:09.710
Yeah, I mean, the scene starts off with them doing this little gag
是啊，我的意思是，这一幕开始时他们演了个小段子，

1402
00:56:09.710 --> 00:56:13.610
of coming in sideways and then moving the screen and all of this.
就是侧着身子进来，然后挪动屏幕之类的。

1403
00:56:13.790 --> 00:56:14.610
And they're giggling.
他们还在咯咯笑。

1404
00:56:15.210 --> 00:56:19.150
Yeah, but then when he finds out that she's not coming back,
没错，但当他发现她不会回来时，

1405
00:56:20.070 --> 00:56:21.330
he's pretty upset.
他非常难过。

1406
00:56:21.730 --> 00:56:24.090
You know, in a table read version of the script,
你知道，在剧本围读版本里，

1407
00:56:24.790 --> 00:56:29.510
Jessica calls his cell phone while he's doing this bit with Erin on the laptop.
当他在笔记本电脑前和艾琳演这段戏时，杰西卡打来了电话。

1408
00:56:30.410 --> 00:56:33.430
And he's kind of like annoyed trying to get Jessica off the line.
他当时有点烦，想赶紧挂掉杰西卡的电话。

1409
00:56:34.550 --> 00:56:35.750
Why, Andy?
为什么，安迪？

1410
00:56:35.910 --> 00:56:36.210
Why?
为什么？

1411
00:56:36.370 --> 00:56:36.810
I don't know.
我不知道。

1412
00:56:36.810 --> 00:56:37.730
Jessica is terrific.
杰西卡很棒。

1413
00:56:38.010 --> 00:56:38.330
I know.
我知道。

1414
00:56:38.510 --> 00:56:40.490
She brings out a great side of you.
她能激发你很好的一面。

1415
00:56:40.670 --> 00:56:41.230
I know.
我知道。

1416
00:56:41.510 --> 00:56:42.470
I don't get it.
我不明白。

1417
00:56:43.190 --> 00:56:45.290
And I guess I would just say, you know what, Jessica,
我想我会说，你知道吗，杰西卡，

1418
00:56:45.470 --> 00:56:48.030
you dodged a bullet because this man doesn't appreciate you.
你躲过了一劫，因为这个男人不懂得珍惜你。

1419
00:56:48.450 --> 00:56:50.410
You don't want to be Mrs. Maybe.
你可不想当“也许太太”。

1420
00:56:51.090 --> 00:56:52.630
No, you don't, Angela.
不，你不想，安吉拉。

1421
00:56:52.630 --> 00:56:53.270
That's right.
没错。

1422
00:56:53.470 --> 00:56:54.990
So get rid of Mr. Maybe.
所以甩掉那个“也许先生”吧。

1423
00:56:55.250 --> 00:56:55.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1424
00:56:56.610 --> 00:56:58.490
So now Jim is on his way to the airport.
现在吉姆正在去机场的路上。

1425
00:56:59.230 --> 00:57:00.530
He's in the car.
他在车里。

1426
00:57:00.690 --> 00:57:01.410
I mean, he's going.
我是说，他正在去。

1427
00:57:01.750 --> 00:57:03.690
Yeah, he's in one of those passenger vans.
对，他坐的是那种客运小巴。

1428
00:57:03.910 --> 00:57:05.670
And Stanley is in the back.
斯坦利也在后面。

1429
00:57:05.670 --> 00:57:07.450
He's kind of slumped towards the window.
他整个人瘫在窗边。

1430
00:57:07.590 --> 00:57:08.330
He's grumpy.
他脾气很坏。

1431
00:57:08.830 --> 00:57:11.210
I mean, he doesn't want to be Scranton Stanley.
我是说，他不想当斯克兰顿的斯坦利。

1432
00:57:11.350 --> 00:57:12.630
He wants to be Florida Stanley.
他想当佛罗里达的斯坦利。

1433
00:57:12.790 --> 00:57:15.030
But Jim's talking to Pam on the phone.
但吉姆正在和帕姆通电话。

1434
00:57:15.030 --> 00:57:19.110
And Pam is kind of saying, Jim, you have to tell Dwight.
帕姆一直在说，吉姆，你必须告诉德怀特。

1435
00:57:19.230 --> 00:57:20.050
You have to.
你必须说。

1436
00:57:20.050 --> 00:57:22.590
And Jim's insisting that he tried.
而吉姆坚持说他试过了。

1437
00:57:22.930 --> 00:57:24.710
And she's like, did you, though?
她说，你真的试了吗？

1438
00:57:25.090 --> 00:57:25.970
Did you try?
你真的努力了吗？

1439
00:57:26.330 --> 00:57:31.270
And I think, you know, this is how I guess it does track.
我觉得，你知道，我想这就是为什么这说得通。

1440
00:57:31.270 --> 00:57:35.830
I mean, how hard did Jim try to get Kathy out of his hotel room?
我是说，吉姆为了让凯西离开他的酒店房间到底有多努力？

1441
00:57:35.850 --> 00:57:38.090
And how hard did he try to tell Dwight this news?
他为了告诉德怀特这个消息又有多努力？

1442
00:57:38.270 --> 00:57:42.010
I mean, Jim's definition of try is pretty weak.
我是说，吉姆对“努力”的定义实在太弱了。

1443
00:57:42.570 --> 00:57:44.790
You know, it was interesting during the scene.
你知道，这一幕很有意思。

1444
00:57:44.950 --> 00:57:47.370
I couldn't help but hear you a little bit.
我忍不住听到了你的一点声音。

1445
00:57:47.770 --> 00:57:48.310
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1446
00:57:48.590 --> 00:57:53.990
Because one of the things you're really good at is sort of understanding how people talk
因为你非常擅长的一点是，理解人们是如何

1447
00:57:53.990 --> 00:57:54.550
to one another.
互相交谈的。

1448
00:57:54.750 --> 00:57:58.970
And so when Pam's like, no, wait, what exactly did Robert say he's going to do?
所以当帕姆说，不，等等，罗伯特到底说他要做什么？

1449
00:57:59.250 --> 00:58:02.290
And Jim's like, I don't know, maybe like give Dwight a talking to.
吉姆说，我不知道，也许就是找德怀特谈谈。

1450
00:58:02.670 --> 00:58:05.990
And Pam very clearly says, Robert doesn't talk like that.
帕姆非常明确地说，罗伯特说话才不是那样。

1451
00:58:06.430 --> 00:58:07.710
He's going to fire him.
他要解雇他。

1452
00:58:08.110 --> 00:58:11.970
And I feel like sometimes, Jenna, like we'll meet someone and I'll be like, oh, yeah.
有时候我觉得，珍娜，我们遇到某个人时，我会觉得，哦，没错。

1453
00:58:12.050 --> 00:58:13.370
And you're like, no, no, no, no.
而你却说，不，不，不，不。

1454
00:58:13.530 --> 00:58:14.250
This is what's happening.
事情就是这样。

1455
00:58:14.470 --> 00:58:15.470
And I'm like, oh, crap.
然后我就想，糟了。

1456
00:58:16.570 --> 00:58:20.350
I don't know if that's totally true, but I think that's a compliment.
我不知道这是否完全属实，但我认为这是一种赞美。

1457
00:58:20.630 --> 00:58:21.150
So I'll take it.
所以我接受了。

1458
00:58:21.150 --> 00:58:22.090
No, it is a compliment.
不，这确实是一种赞美。

1459
00:58:22.250 --> 00:58:25.910
I think you're good at cutting through the BS and seeing what's really happening.
我觉得你很擅长看穿废话，看到事情的真相。

1460
00:58:26.290 --> 00:58:30.490
Well, Jim is going to ultimately promise Pam, okay, I'll tell Dwight.
好吧，吉姆最终会答应帕姆，好吧，我会告诉德怀特。

1461
00:58:31.110 --> 00:58:35.130
And thus begins something that I found very odd.
于是开始了一件我觉得非常奇怪的事情。

1462
00:58:35.130 --> 00:58:36.350
I'll talk about it later.
我稍后再说。

1463
00:58:36.770 --> 00:58:37.170
What?
什么？

1464
00:58:37.710 --> 00:58:38.630
I'll talk about it later.
我稍后再说。

1465
00:58:38.830 --> 00:58:39.070
Oh.
哦。

1466
00:58:39.330 --> 00:58:39.770
It's okay.
没关系。

1467
00:58:40.470 --> 00:58:41.930
I'll bring it up when we get there.
等我们说到那儿的时候我再提。

1468
00:58:42.130 --> 00:58:42.670
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

1469
00:58:43.590 --> 00:58:45.190
Basically, okay, I'll just say it.
基本上，好吧，我还是直说吧。

1470
00:58:45.290 --> 00:58:46.270
Because now I'm curious.
因为我现在很好奇。

1471
00:58:46.430 --> 00:58:46.770
I know.
我知道。

1472
00:58:46.870 --> 00:58:47.610
And you don't want to wait.
而且你不想等。

1473
00:58:47.790 --> 00:58:49.170
Okay, I don't want you to have to guess.
好吧，我不想让你去猜。

1474
00:58:50.130 --> 00:58:51.410
Stanley can't go to the airport?
斯坦利不能去机场吗？

1475
00:58:51.870 --> 00:58:54.650
Why does Stanley wait to go to the airport too?
为什么斯坦利也要等去机场？

1476
00:58:54.950 --> 00:58:56.810
Oh, because they're in the same passenger van.
哦，因为他们坐的是同一辆客货车。

1477
00:58:56.810 --> 00:58:57.990
They're in the same passenger van.
他们坐的是同一辆客货车。

1478
00:58:58.150 --> 00:58:59.870
How does this all go down?
这一切是怎么发生的？

1479
00:59:00.590 --> 00:59:03.590
Jim's going to turn around the whole passenger van with Stanley in it.
吉姆要让载着斯坦利的整辆客货车掉头。

1480
00:59:04.050 --> 00:59:05.430
Stanley doesn't want to leave Florida.
斯坦利不想离开佛罗里达。

1481
00:59:05.590 --> 00:59:07.450
Do you think he cares if he takes a detour?
你觉得他在乎绕路吗？

1482
00:59:07.710 --> 00:59:08.790
Okay, all right.
好吧，行。

1483
00:59:08.890 --> 00:59:09.450
I'll buy that.
我信了。

1484
00:59:09.610 --> 00:59:09.950
Thank you.
谢谢。

1485
00:59:10.070 --> 00:59:12.450
He probably went to the hotel bar and is having a cocktail.
他可能去了酒店酒吧，正在喝鸡尾酒。

1486
00:59:12.710 --> 00:59:12.970
You're right.
你说得对。

1487
00:59:13.630 --> 00:59:17.610
Back in Scranton, Toby and Daryl are really going at it now.
回到斯克兰顿，托比和达里尔现在真的杠上了。

1488
00:59:17.730 --> 00:59:21.490
They're campaigning super hard to win Kevin's cookie business.
他们正在拼命拉票，想赢得凯文的饼干生意。

1489
00:59:21.490 --> 00:59:24.410
And the whole bullpen is just sitting around watching.
整个办公区的人都坐着看热闹。

1490
00:59:24.690 --> 00:59:26.970
They're shouting out different things they have to do.
他们大声喊出他们必须做的各种事情。

1491
00:59:27.370 --> 00:59:29.690
The whole workday has stopped for this.
整个工作日都因为这个停摆了。

1492
00:59:29.830 --> 00:59:30.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1493
00:59:30.190 --> 00:59:31.930
They're like, you have to kiss Meredith.
他们说，你必须亲吻梅雷迪思。

1494
00:59:32.250 --> 00:59:32.690
You have to.
你必须亲。

1495
00:59:32.810 --> 00:59:33.670
What are all the other things?
还有其他什么要求？

1496
00:59:33.690 --> 00:59:35.510
They have to sing a song for him.
他们必须为他唱首歌。

1497
00:59:36.150 --> 00:59:38.990
I've got some surprising news about that song.
关于那首歌我有个惊人的消息。

1498
00:59:39.270 --> 00:59:40.870
Guess how much it cost us?
猜猜我们花了多少钱？

1499
00:59:41.510 --> 00:59:42.430
Four dollars.
四美元。

1500
00:59:43.010 --> 00:59:43.790
Zero dollars.
零美元。

1501
00:59:43.870 --> 00:59:44.090
Oh!
噢！

1502
00:59:44.290 --> 00:59:44.670
Zero.
零。

1503
00:59:44.930 --> 00:59:46.150
It was public domain.
那是公有领域的内容。

1504
00:59:47.050 --> 00:59:48.590
We got it for nothing.
我们没花钱就拿到了。

1505
00:59:49.150 --> 00:59:51.070
Well, nothing is really resolved here.
好吧，这里什么问题都没解决。

1506
00:59:51.190 --> 00:59:52.330
He hasn't picked a winner.
他还没选出赢家。

1507
00:59:52.530 --> 00:59:58.610
And they threaten to stop competing for his business until he reveals he's prepared to order triple digits.
他们威胁说，除非他透露自己准备订购三位数的数量，否则就不再竞争他的业务。

1508
00:59:58.610 --> 00:59:59.210
Yeah.
是啊。

1509
00:59:59.870 --> 01:00:06.650
Well, remember how our writer, Robert, told me there was this Pam-Kevin storyline in his original outline?
嗯，还记得我们的编剧罗伯特跟我说过，他最初的大纲里有帕姆和凯文的故事线吗？

1510
01:00:06.930 --> 01:00:08.910
It would have culminated with this.
原本会以这个情节告终。

1511
01:00:09.090 --> 01:00:12.790
Pam becomes concerned that Kevin is being taken advantage of.
帕姆开始担心凯文被人占便宜了。

1512
01:00:13.090 --> 01:00:13.510
Okay.
好吧。

1513
01:00:13.710 --> 01:00:17.170
That he really doesn't need to buy 100 boxes of cookies.
担心他其实根本没必要买100盒饼干。

1514
01:00:17.730 --> 01:00:22.430
So she decides she will not buy her two boxes of Thin Mints,
所以她决定自己也不买那两盒薄荷巧克力饼干了，

1515
01:00:22.590 --> 01:00:27.430
which is equally hard for her if Kevin doesn't buy his 100 boxes.
如果凯文不买那100盒，这对她来说也同样艰难。

1516
01:00:27.430 --> 01:00:28.690
She's like, Kevin, come on.
她当时就像是，凯文，拜托。

1517
01:00:28.830 --> 01:00:30.190
We're going to make this pack together.
我们要一起遵守这个约定。

1518
01:00:31.030 --> 01:00:36.050
And that solidarity gives Kevin the strength to not buy any cookies at all.
而那种团结一致给了凯文力量，让他最终一盒饼干都没买。

1519
01:00:36.270 --> 01:00:37.030
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

1520
01:00:37.030 --> 01:00:40.890
So the episode would have ended with Kevin buying nothing.
所以那一集原本会以凯文什么都没买而结束。

1521
01:00:41.250 --> 01:00:41.570
Yeah.
是啊。

1522
01:00:41.750 --> 01:00:44.870
Kevin would have made the choice that he doesn't need 100 boxes of cookies,
凯文会做出选择，意识到他并不需要100盒饼干，

1523
01:00:44.870 --> 01:00:48.130
not because he loses the favor of Daryl and Toby.
而不是因为他失去了达里尔和托比的青睐。

1524
01:00:48.650 --> 01:00:49.670
I kind of like it.
我挺喜欢这个设定的。

1525
01:00:49.950 --> 01:00:50.670
I know.
我知道。

1526
01:00:50.670 --> 01:00:56.490
And what Robert said he really liked is that it was just as hard for Pam to give up her two boxes of Thin Mints
罗伯特说他特别喜欢的一点是，帕姆放弃她的两盒薄荷巧克力饼干，

1527
01:00:56.490 --> 01:01:00.030
as it was for Kevin to give up 100 boxes of cookies.
和凯文放弃那100盒饼干一样艰难。

1528
01:01:00.650 --> 01:01:07.350
Well, back at Sabre, Jim rushes in to tell Dwight about Robert's plan, but Dwight doesn't believe him.
回到赛博公司，吉姆冲进去告诉德怀特关于罗伯特的计划，但德怀特不相信他。

1529
01:01:07.610 --> 01:01:07.910
No.
不。

1530
01:01:08.250 --> 01:01:11.850
He says nothing is going to stop him, which is the mark of a great man.
他说什么都阻止不了他，这正是一个伟大人物的标志。

1531
01:01:12.030 --> 01:01:14.870
Dunder Mifflin, the farm, Moe's, they're in his rearview mirror.
邓德·米夫林、农场、莫氏酒吧，这些都已成为他的过去式。

1532
01:01:15.070 --> 01:01:16.830
He has a date with destiny.
他要去赴命运之约了。

1533
01:01:17.070 --> 01:01:20.590
We had a fan question about this, Angela, from Amberlee B.
安吉拉，我们收到一个关于此事的粉丝提问，来自佛罗里达州的安珀莉·B。

1534
01:01:20.750 --> 01:01:21.250
in Florida,
她说，我一直不明白德怀特怎么会这么轻易就准备抛下斯克兰顿。

1535
01:01:21.250 --> 01:01:25.870
who said, I have never understood how Dwight is so ready to leave behind Scranton.
他曾经说过，他的人生目标之一就是死在邓德·米夫林的办公椅上。

1536
01:01:26.010 --> 01:01:31.750
He once said one of his life goals was to die in his desk chair at Dunder Mifflin.
是啊。

1537
01:01:31.850 --> 01:01:32.010
Yeah.
还有他的甜菜农场，那是他家族传承了几代的产业。

1538
01:01:32.370 --> 01:01:36.330
Also, his beet farm, which has been passed down in his family for generations.
他投入了那么多时间在上面。

1539
01:01:36.750 --> 01:01:38.730
He's devoted so much time to it.
他热爱在那里的生活。

1540
01:01:38.810 --> 01:01:40.010
He loves living out there.
对他来说，放弃这一切似乎代价太大了。

1541
01:01:40.730 --> 01:01:43.150
It seems like a lot for him to leave behind.
谈谈看。

1542
01:01:43.610 --> 01:01:44.130
Discuss.
嗯，安珀莉，我觉得这是一个很好的问题，我非常理解你的意思。

1543
01:01:44.730 --> 01:01:48.850
Well, Amberlee, I think this is a great question, and I really hear what you mean.
我能想到的就是，德怀特一直渴望得到这个头衔，某种头衔。

1544
01:01:49.230 --> 01:01:57.910
All I can think of is that Dwight has yearned for this title, some kind of title.
这给了他一种自信和自我价值感。

1545
01:01:58.510 --> 01:02:02.050
It's given him a sense of confidence, self-worth.
这是他长期以来一直努力追求的东西。

1546
01:02:02.250 --> 01:02:05.510
It's been this thing he's been working towards for so long.
我觉得在那个当下，这让他模糊了一些对他而言真正重要的东西，

1547
01:02:05.650 --> 01:02:10.230
And I think in the moment, it's blurred some of the things that really mean a lot to him
因为他渴望这个头衔太久了，无论是副总裁还是分公司经理，不管是什么。

1548
01:02:10.230 --> 01:02:17.530
because he's wanted it for so long, this title, this VP or branch manager, whatever it was.
这可是这家公司的头衔。

1549
01:02:17.690 --> 01:02:19.010
It's a title at this company.
是啊。

1550
01:02:19.390 --> 01:02:19.810
Yeah.
是啊。

1551
01:02:19.990 --> 01:02:23.710
I think that his ambition is blinding him here.
我觉得他的野心让他失去了理智。

1552
01:02:23.990 --> 01:02:24.210
Yeah.
没错。

1553
01:02:24.910 --> 01:02:28.230
Nothing Jim says works, so he's decided to just tackle Dwight.
吉姆说什么都没用，所以他决定直接扑倒德怀特。

1554
01:02:28.550 --> 01:02:28.770
Yeah.
是啊。

1555
01:02:28.950 --> 01:02:30.310
Just tackle him to the ground.
直接把他扑倒在地。

1556
01:02:30.730 --> 01:02:35.050
And look all of a sudden who has pain in his appendix stitches.
结果你看，他阑尾手术的伤口突然就疼了。

1557
01:02:35.570 --> 01:02:36.170
Yes.
没错。

1558
01:02:36.510 --> 01:02:36.790
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1559
01:02:37.510 --> 01:02:41.190
Didn't seem to bother him when he was going after the bed bugs.
他去抓臭虫的时候可没见他觉得疼。

1560
01:02:41.390 --> 01:02:41.590
Nope.
确实。

1561
01:02:41.710 --> 01:02:44.490
He could dive into a bed and roll around in some sheets.
他当时还能往床上扑，在床单上滚来滚去。

1562
01:02:44.670 --> 01:02:47.470
But when he got tackled, he was like, oh, my appendix.
可一旦被扑倒，他就开始喊哎哟，我的阑尾。

1563
01:02:47.770 --> 01:02:48.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1564
01:02:48.430 --> 01:02:54.090
Well, I think Dwight was faking a little bit because he's going to rev up, and he's going
嗯，我觉得德怀特有点装模作样，因为他准备蓄力，打算

1565
01:02:54.090 --> 01:02:56.870
to try to charge Jim.
冲向吉姆。

1566
01:02:57.270 --> 01:03:00.170
He's going to go up the wall a little bit, and then he falls.
他先是往墙上蹭了蹭，然后就摔倒了。

1567
01:03:00.470 --> 01:03:04.910
I thought it was so funny when he started doing his little foot back and forth motion on the
我觉得他开始在地毯上做那种双脚来回摩擦的动作时特别好笑，吉姆当时就像在说，我知道你在搞什么鬼。

1568
01:03:04.910 --> 01:03:07.010
carpet, Jim was like, I know what you're doing.
是啊。

1569
01:03:07.170 --> 01:03:07.470
Yeah.
那招没用。

1570
01:03:07.670 --> 01:03:08.390
It doesn't work.
这让我想起两兄弟，他们太了解彼此了。

1571
01:03:09.110 --> 01:03:12.890
This is when they reminded me of two brothers that just know each other so well.
哦，确实。

1572
01:03:13.070 --> 01:03:13.650
Oh, yeah.
观察得真准。

1573
01:03:13.770 --> 01:03:15.090
That's such a good observation.
我们收到了很多关于这场打斗的粉丝来信。

1574
01:03:15.790 --> 01:03:18.010
So we got a lot of fan mail about this fight.
大家想知道他们是在闹着玩，还是提前编排好的。

1575
01:03:18.150 --> 01:03:22.810
People wanted to know if they were just playing around or if it was choreographed.
我联系了史蒂夫·伯吉斯，他提醒我，其实

1576
01:03:23.150 --> 01:03:29.570
And I reached out to Steve Burgess, and, you know, he reminded me that this was actually
这里的动作都是经过精心设计的，而且是和我们的特技

1577
01:03:29.570 --> 01:03:35.230
the action here was meticulously scripted, and that it was all worked out with our stunt
协调员布雷特·琼斯一起敲定的。

1578
01:03:35.230 --> 01:03:36.310
coordinator, Brett Jones.
全都是编排好的。

1579
01:03:36.430 --> 01:03:37.610
It was all choreographed.
他说在拍一些特写镜头时，我们在地上铺了防摔垫，然后

1580
01:03:37.710 --> 01:03:41.790
He said for some of the close-up shots, we had fall pads on the ground, and then they
在拍远景时把垫子撤掉。

1581
01:03:41.790 --> 01:03:43.670
would pull them out for the wider shots.
但他们演得太好了，看起来就像是即兴发生的冲突一样。

1582
01:03:43.810 --> 01:03:49.390
But they did such a great job of making it look like it was just happening in the moment.
罗伯特·帕德尼克说，吉姆和德怀特之间的这一幕是他

1583
01:03:49.930 --> 01:03:53.730
Robert Padnick said this moment between Jim and Dwight was one of the highlights for
这一集里的高光时刻之一。

1584
01:03:53.730 --> 01:03:54.630
him of the episode.
我翻看了剧本，找出了罗伯特写的所有

1585
01:03:55.330 --> 01:04:00.550
Well, I went to the script, and I pulled out all of the stage directions that Robert
舞台动作说明，他们真的完美地执行了这些动作。

1586
01:04:00.550 --> 01:04:05.250
wrote, and they really executed them perfectly.
我们应该读一读，因为写得太详细了。

1587
01:04:05.770 --> 01:04:07.990
We should read them because they're so detailed.
我知道。

1588
01:04:08.210 --> 01:04:08.650
I know.
好的。

1589
01:04:08.750 --> 01:04:08.950
Okay.
那么，这就是所有剧本里的动作说明。

1590
01:04:09.170 --> 01:04:11.230
So here are all of the scripted actions.
从这里开始。

1591
01:04:11.410 --> 01:04:12.510
It starts with this.
吉姆把德怀特从会议室拖到了另一个房间。

1592
01:04:13.030 --> 01:04:16.890
Jim has dragged Dwight away from the conference room into another room.
德怀特紧贴着墙，吉姆拉扯着他。

1593
01:04:17.190 --> 01:04:20.010
Dwight clings to the wall as Jim pulls on him.
吉姆用手捂住德怀特的嘴，阻止他大喊大叫。

1594
01:04:20.410 --> 01:04:23.570
Jim puts his hand over Dwight's mouth to stop him from yelling.
过了一会儿，他松开了手。

1595
01:04:23.570 --> 01:04:25.550
After a moment, he pulls away.
德怀特开始踢吉姆的裆部。

1596
01:04:26.210 --> 01:04:28.630
Dwight starts kicking at Jim's crotch.
吉姆用力拽他。

1597
01:04:28.910 --> 01:04:30.470
Jim tugs on him harder.
等等，我不记得有这一段。

1598
01:04:30.710 --> 01:04:32.110
Now, I don't remember that part.
现在到了他要模仿公牛的那部分，剧本上写着，依然弯着腰，

1599
01:04:33.710 --> 01:04:38.530
Now we get to the part where he's supposed to act like a bull, and it says, still doubled
德怀特像公牛一样冲向吉姆。

1600
01:04:38.530 --> 01:04:41.010
over, Dwight charges Jim like a bull.
没错。

1601
01:04:41.670 --> 01:04:44.030
Dwight starts scuffing his foot on the floor.
德怀特开始在地上蹭脚。

1602
01:04:44.270 --> 01:04:45.970
Then he starts running in place.
接着他开始原地跑动。

1603
01:04:46.410 --> 01:04:49.070
Dwight charges at Jim, then veers at the last second.
德怀特冲向吉姆，在最后一秒又转向避开了。

1604
01:04:49.270 --> 01:04:53.110
He tries to run up the wall and over Jim, but crashes to the ground.
他试图跑上墙壁越过吉姆，结果摔倒在地。

1605
01:04:54.110 --> 01:04:55.490
It continues, guys.
还没完呢，伙计们。

1606
01:04:55.750 --> 01:04:56.870
You think you're done there.
你们以为这就结束了。

1607
01:04:56.990 --> 01:04:57.190
No.
并没有。

1608
01:04:57.590 --> 01:05:00.550
It says, Dwight and Jim, both tired, continue to tussle.
上面写着，德怀特和吉姆，两人都很疲惫，继续扭打在一起。

1609
01:05:00.730 --> 01:05:02.510
Dwight is arduously dragging Jim.
德怀特费力地拖着吉姆。

1610
01:05:02.750 --> 01:05:03.950
He stops exhausted.
他累得停了下来。

1611
01:05:04.950 --> 01:05:07.870
Then it says, Dwight pokes a finger into Jim's kidney.
然后上面写着，德怀特用手指戳了戳吉姆的肾脏部位。

1612
01:05:08.130 --> 01:05:08.890
I don't remember that.
我不记得有这一段。

1613
01:05:08.890 --> 01:05:09.670
I don't think that happened.
我觉得没发生过这种事。

1614
01:05:09.970 --> 01:05:12.210
Maybe it did, though, and we cut it down.
不过也许确实发生过，只是我们剪掉了。

1615
01:05:12.410 --> 01:05:14.190
Maybe this was a bigger fight for them.
也许对他们来说，这原本是一场更激烈的打斗。

1616
01:05:14.610 --> 01:05:18.910
It says that Dwight lifts Jim up but can only get him a few inches off the ground.
上面写着德怀特抱起吉姆，但只能让他离地几英寸。

1617
01:05:18.910 --> 01:05:20.090
I liked that detail.
我喜欢这个细节。

1618
01:05:20.090 --> 01:05:20.830
That was funny.
那很有趣。

1619
01:05:21.030 --> 01:05:22.310
He slams him down.
他把吉姆重重地摔在地上。

1620
01:05:22.510 --> 01:05:25.310
By the way, I loved it when Jim grabbed the plant.
顺便说一句，我很喜欢吉姆抓起盆栽的那一幕。

1621
01:05:25.330 --> 01:05:28.070
That's not in the direction, but it cracked me up.
剧本里没写，但那真的把我逗乐了。

1622
01:05:28.290 --> 01:05:28.470
Yeah.
是啊。

1623
01:05:30.690 --> 01:05:36.270
Basically, it ends with them both on the ground and Dwight rolling over and getting up with
基本上，结尾是两人都倒在地上，德怀特翻身起来，

1624
01:05:36.270 --> 01:05:38.010
a groan, it says.
伴随着一声呻吟，剧本上是这么写的。

1625
01:05:38.530 --> 01:05:39.790
Jim stays on the ground.
吉姆留在地上。

1626
01:05:39.790 --> 01:05:40.430
He's done.
他彻底不行了。

1627
01:05:40.570 --> 01:05:41.030
He tried.
他尽力了。

1628
01:05:41.810 --> 01:05:43.610
Now that is trying.
那才叫尽力。

1629
01:05:44.590 --> 01:05:45.710
Okay, Pam.
好了，帕姆。

1630
01:05:45.710 --> 01:05:46.270
Okay.
好的。

1631
01:05:46.530 --> 01:05:49.570
I just want to say, now you can say you've tried.
我只是想说，现在你可以说你已经尽力了。

1632
01:05:50.370 --> 01:05:55.590
Well, while all of this was going on, there would have been a scene inside the boardroom.
嗯，在这一切发生的同时，会议室里原本还有一场戏。

1633
01:05:55.590 --> 01:05:57.030
It was in the shooting draft.
那是在拍摄剧本里的。

1634
01:05:57.030 --> 01:05:57.970
We did shoot it.
我们确实拍了。

1635
01:05:58.050 --> 01:05:59.270
It's in deleted scenes.
在删减片段里。

1636
01:06:00.010 --> 01:06:03.330
And Todd Packer is going to try to bond with Robert California.
托德·帕克试图和罗伯特·加利福尼亚套近乎。

1637
01:06:03.850 --> 01:06:07.250
Oh, yeah, because they're all in there, and they're like, where's Dwight?
哦，对，因为他们都在里面，然后他们问，德怀特去哪了？

1638
01:06:07.490 --> 01:06:08.330
Yeah, they're just waiting.
是啊，他们就在那等着。

1639
01:06:08.330 --> 01:06:08.510
What's going on?
怎么回事？

1640
01:06:08.510 --> 01:06:09.670
Why aren't we starting this?
为什么还不开始？

1641
01:06:09.870 --> 01:06:10.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1642
01:06:10.630 --> 01:06:15.110
Well, Jenna, you might have a soulmate in Robert California because here's what happened.
嗯，珍娜，你可能在罗伯特·加利福尼亚身上找到了知音，因为事情是这样的。

1643
01:06:15.910 --> 01:06:18.790
The shooting draft read, the board has gathered.
拍摄剧本上写着，董事会已经集合完毕。

1644
01:06:19.010 --> 01:06:21.650
The current slide reads, what's in store?
当前的幻灯片上写着，接下来有什么？

1645
01:06:22.110 --> 01:06:25.710
Robert sits contentedly awaiting what's to come.
罗伯特心满意足地坐着，等待着即将发生的事情。

1646
01:06:26.390 --> 01:06:28.490
Packer sidles up next to him.
帕克凑到他身边。

1647
01:06:29.010 --> 01:06:31.470
Packer says, amped for thrones?
帕克说，对《权力的游戏》兴奋吗？

1648
01:06:32.450 --> 01:06:37.390
Off of Robert's blank look, Packer says, game of thrones.
看到罗伯特一脸茫然，帕克解释说，就是HBO的那个剧《权力的游戏》。

1649
01:06:37.810 --> 01:06:39.390
There's a long beat.
沉默了很久。

1650
01:06:39.830 --> 01:06:42.850
Packer says, it's a show on HBO.
帕克说，是HBO的一部剧。

1651
01:06:42.850 --> 01:06:43.030
No.
不。

1652
01:06:43.450 --> 01:06:45.110
Robert says, oh, no.
罗伯特说，噢，不。

1653
01:06:46.130 --> 01:06:47.810
Packer slinks away.
帕克溜走了。

1654
01:06:50.760 --> 01:06:52.560
Oh, Robert.
噢，罗伯特。

1655
01:06:53.020 --> 01:06:58.160
Look, Jenna, there's someone else that's not as into sort of fantasy stuff.
你看，珍娜，还有别人也不怎么喜欢那种奇幻的东西。

1656
01:06:58.720 --> 01:06:59.600
I know.
我知道。

1657
01:06:59.840 --> 01:07:01.360
Maybe he would have loved The Edge.
也许他会喜欢《边缘》的。

1658
01:07:03.420 --> 01:07:05.220
I think he would have, actually.
我觉得他其实会喜欢的。

1659
01:07:05.720 --> 01:07:07.200
I think he really would have.
我觉得他真的会喜欢。

1660
01:07:07.640 --> 01:07:12.020
As it turns out, Packer is going to take over the role of VP.
事实证明，帕克要接任副总裁一职了。

1661
01:07:12.240 --> 01:07:14.020
He's going to do the presentation with Nellie.
他要和内莉一起做演示。

1662
01:07:14.140 --> 01:07:17.640
Yeah, he knows it forwards and backwards and doggy style.
是啊，他对此了如指掌，甚至连那些下流的细节都一清二楚。

1663
01:07:17.860 --> 01:07:18.760
He's ready to go.
他准备好了。

1664
01:07:18.760 --> 01:07:25.220
And as promised, Robert is going to tank it and fire Packer.
正如承诺的那样，罗伯特打算搞砸演示并解雇帕克。

1665
01:07:25.420 --> 01:07:25.860
Yeah.
没错。

1666
01:07:26.120 --> 01:07:28.080
Just as Dwight is walking in the door.
就在德怀特走进门的时候。

1667
01:07:28.420 --> 01:07:31.520
He hears this and he realizes Jim was right.
他听到了这些，意识到吉姆是对的。

1668
01:07:31.720 --> 01:07:33.820
Jim really was trying to save his job.
吉姆确实是在试图保住他的工作。

1669
01:07:34.040 --> 01:07:34.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1670
01:07:34.720 --> 01:07:38.280
My second favorite line of this episode happened in this scene.
这一集中我第二喜欢的台词就出现在这一幕。

1671
01:07:38.800 --> 01:07:43.520
Nellie says, whatever you do, do not blame Todd Packer.
内莉说，无论你做什么，都不要责怪托德·帕克。

1672
01:07:43.520 --> 01:07:45.380
It is not his fault.
这不是他的错。

1673
01:07:45.720 --> 01:07:51.360
Blame his upbringing, his parents, the society that would mold this idiotic creature.
要怪就怪他的成长环境、他的父母，以及那个塑造了这个白痴生物的社会。

1674
01:07:51.740 --> 01:07:55.800
Fire the employee, yes, but not the man.
解雇员工可以，但不要否定他这个人。

1675
01:07:56.080 --> 01:07:58.560
You may not cancel his soul.
你不能抹杀他的灵魂。

1676
01:07:58.900 --> 01:08:03.040
And then Robert California says, that was never on the table.
然后罗伯特·加利福尼亚说，那从来都不在考虑范围内。

1677
01:08:03.960 --> 01:08:05.320
It's cracked me up.
这把我逗乐了。

1678
01:08:09.360 --> 01:08:12.740
Dwight's going to leave the conference room and he's going to have a nice moment with Jim.
德怀特要离开会议室了，他会和吉姆有一个不错的互动时刻。

1679
01:08:12.740 --> 01:08:15.620
He's going to realize Jim really was being his friend.
他会意识到吉姆确实是在把他当朋友。

1680
01:08:15.840 --> 01:08:20.880
It's a really sweet kind of moment in the hallway offers Jim his hand to help him up off the ground.
走廊里有一个非常温馨的时刻，他向吉姆伸出手，想把他从地上拉起来。

1681
01:08:21.040 --> 01:08:21.820
Jim hasn't moved.
吉姆没动。

1682
01:08:22.100 --> 01:08:22.960
He's very tired.
他太累了。

1683
01:08:23.840 --> 01:08:28.220
I saw a few people write in and say they wondered if this was a turning point for Jim and Dwight.
我看到一些人写信说，他们想知道这是否是吉姆和德怀特关系的一个转折点。

1684
01:08:29.200 --> 01:08:30.500
Yeah, that's true.
是啊，确实如此。

1685
01:08:30.880 --> 01:08:36.160
There were people who remembered what Grant Daniels said about how Jim and Dwight were never to become friends.
有些人还记得格兰特·丹尼尔斯说过吉姆和德怀特永远不会成为朋友。

1686
01:08:36.160 --> 01:08:44.400
But they thought there have been a couple of nods in the last few episodes, them having their desserts in Florida and then this moment in Florida.
但他们认为在过去几集中已经有了一些暗示，比如他们在佛罗里达一起吃甜点，然后就是佛罗里达的这一刻。

1687
01:08:44.680 --> 01:08:44.840
Yep.
没错。

1688
01:08:45.140 --> 01:08:45.580
Don't worry.
别担心。

1689
01:08:45.720 --> 01:08:46.400
They'll fight again.
他们还会再打起来的。

1690
01:08:47.020 --> 01:08:51.180
Well, now the Saber Florida crew are going to arrive back to Scranton.
好了，现在赛博佛罗里达团队要回到斯克兰顿了。

1691
01:08:51.420 --> 01:08:52.580
They walk in.
他们走了进来。

1692
01:08:52.780 --> 01:08:54.140
Stanley, Dwight, Jim.
斯坦利、德怀特、吉姆。

1693
01:08:54.620 --> 01:08:56.220
Everyone's excited to see them.
每个人都很高兴见到他们。

1694
01:08:56.560 --> 01:08:58.420
Pam seems surprised.
帕姆看起来很惊讶。

1695
01:08:59.020 --> 01:09:00.820
She's like, hey, stranger.
她就像是说，嘿，陌生人。

1696
01:09:01.100 --> 01:09:03.240
Then they make out in front of everyone.
然后他们在大家面前亲热起来。

1697
01:09:03.240 --> 01:09:06.020
I just wrote, awkward, what the hell is happening?
我当时只写了：尴尬，这到底是怎么回事？

1698
01:09:06.260 --> 01:09:08.420
Is this Jim's first time seeing Pam?
这是吉姆第一次见到帕姆吗？

1699
01:09:08.600 --> 01:09:09.860
Had they not been texting?
他们之前没发过短信吗？

1700
01:09:09.940 --> 01:09:11.380
She seems surprised.
她看起来很惊讶。

1701
01:09:11.880 --> 01:09:13.060
Now they're making out.
现在他们正在亲热。

1702
01:09:13.280 --> 01:09:13.860
What the heck?
搞什么鬼？

1703
01:09:14.180 --> 01:09:16.320
Well, Angela, Mila P.
嗯，安吉拉，来自德克萨斯州休斯顿的米拉·P。

1704
01:09:16.540 --> 01:09:23.100
from Houston, Texas was also confused and wondered, Pam is so shocked to see Jim.
也很困惑，她想知道，帕姆看到吉姆时为什么那么震惊。

1705
01:09:23.100 --> 01:09:28.320
How is it possible that a wife doesn't know her husband is coming back home after being gone for a while?
一个妻子怎么可能不知道自己的丈夫在离家一段时间后要回家了呢？

1706
01:09:29.140 --> 01:09:31.040
Also, Savannah M.
还有，来自犹他州盐湖城的萨凡纳·M。

1707
01:09:31.160 --> 01:09:32.860
from Salt Lake City, Utah said,
说道，

1708
01:09:33.520 --> 01:09:37.620
Why did the Florida team come back to the office rather than go home?
为什么佛罗里达团队回到办公室而不是直接回家？

1709
01:09:37.800 --> 01:09:42.560
It seems weird to bring all their luggage to the office rather than have the rest of the day off.
带着所有行李回办公室，而不是享受剩下的假期，这看起来很奇怪。

1710
01:09:42.740 --> 01:09:43.980
And Anna L.
还有来自西班牙格拉纳达，现在住在爱尔兰科克的安娜·L。

1711
01:09:44.200 --> 01:09:47.820
from Granada, Spain, who is now living in Cork, Ireland, said,
说道，

1712
01:09:47.960 --> 01:09:50.680
How many hours did this day have?
这一天到底有多少个小时？

1713
01:09:50.680 --> 01:09:56.000
They started playing golf, had a meeting about Sabre, Dwight and Jim got in a fight,
他们先是去打高尔夫，开了关于赛博公司的会，德怀特和吉姆还打了一架，

1714
01:09:56.240 --> 01:10:02.840
and still took a flight from Tallahassee to Scranton to arrive back at the office before 5 p.m.
结果还能赶上从塔拉哈西飞往斯克兰顿的航班，并在下午5点前回到办公室。

1715
01:10:03.500 --> 01:10:04.700
That's a good point.
说得好。

1716
01:10:05.060 --> 01:10:09.420
And by the way, I want to say, Anna, I looked it up,
顺便说一下，安娜，我查过了，

1717
01:10:09.500 --> 01:10:13.760
and it is an almost four-hour flight from Tallahassee to Scranton.
从塔拉哈西飞往斯克兰顿的航班飞行时间差不多要四个小时。

1718
01:10:14.450 --> 01:10:16.240
This is what I wrote down, Angela.
安吉拉，这是我写下来的疑问。

1719
01:10:16.840 --> 01:10:19.340
How is Jim arriving back with Stanley?
吉姆是怎么和斯坦利一起回来的？

1720
01:10:19.540 --> 01:10:21.180
Weren't they on an earlier flight?
他们不是应该坐更早的航班吗？

1721
01:10:21.400 --> 01:10:24.200
Why wouldn't Stanley have just flown on his original flight?
为什么斯坦利不直接坐他原来的航班回来？

1722
01:10:24.500 --> 01:10:29.100
Also, Dwight didn't even have a plane ticket home because he thought he was staying in Florida.
而且，德怀特甚至都没有回家的机票，因为他以为自己要留在佛罗里达。

1723
01:10:29.340 --> 01:10:35.410
How did the three of them all wind up on the same flight out of Florida and make it back by 5 p.m.?
他们三个人是怎么凑到同一班离开佛罗里达的飞机，并赶在下午5点前回来的？

1724
01:10:35.410 --> 01:10:39.450
And also, wouldn't Pam pick him up at the airport?
还有，帕姆难道不应该去机场接他吗？

1725
01:10:39.750 --> 01:10:41.290
Or wouldn't she be like,
或者她难道不该说，

1726
01:10:41.650 --> 01:10:47.430
Honey, you were supposed to come home three hours ago on that other flight that you told me you were coming home on?
亲爱的，你不是应该在三小时前就坐你告诉我的那趟航班到家了吗？

1727
01:10:47.550 --> 01:10:47.830
No.
没有。

1728
01:10:47.970 --> 01:10:49.330
She's like, hey, stranger.
她却说，嘿，陌生人。

1729
01:10:50.530 --> 01:10:54.950
Well, you know, it had been a long time since Jim and Pam had been scripted to do a kiss.
嗯，你知道，吉姆和帕姆已经很久没有被安排吻戏了。

1730
01:10:55.070 --> 01:10:55.450
Oh, yeah.
哦，确实。

1731
01:10:55.590 --> 01:10:58.890
And for whatever reason, John and I, we just kept breaking.
不管什么原因，我和约翰当时一直笑场。

1732
01:10:59.350 --> 01:11:02.910
I think it was also because Ed was, like, right over our shoulder.
我觉得也是因为艾德当时就在我们肩膀后面。

1733
01:11:02.910 --> 01:11:04.490
Andy is right there.
安迪就在那儿。

1734
01:11:04.490 --> 01:11:08.290
He's supposed to, I guess, take in the moment, get inspired to go get Aaron.
我想他本该沉浸在那个时刻，受到启发去追艾琳。

1735
01:11:08.550 --> 01:11:12.990
But it's so awkward because he's just a little head bobbing behind you.
但那太尴尬了，因为他就在你们身后探头探脑的。

1736
01:11:13.110 --> 01:11:15.290
Well, there's a bunch of bloopers of that moment.
那个瞬间有很多NG镜头。

1737
01:11:15.290 --> 01:11:16.150
I'll tell you that.
我跟你说。

1738
01:11:16.850 --> 01:11:22.330
Andy's now going to have this talking head where he says, I'm going to Florida, you know, going to go get Aaron.
安迪接下来会有个采访镜头，他说，我要去佛罗里达，你知道，去把艾琳追回来。

1739
01:11:22.490 --> 01:11:23.450
It's crazy, right?
太疯狂了，对吧？

1740
01:11:23.750 --> 01:11:28.050
And he's trying to shut off his computer, but he has all these tabs open and it's moving slowly.
他正试图关掉电脑，但他开了太多标签页，电脑运行得很慢。

1741
01:11:29.150 --> 01:11:30.270
What the hell's happening?
到底在搞什么鬼？

1742
01:11:30.610 --> 01:11:32.010
He has a ring.
他有一枚戒指。

1743
01:11:32.010 --> 01:11:33.970
He's ready to propose to Jessica.
他准备向杰西卡求婚。

1744
01:11:34.330 --> 01:11:34.730
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1745
01:11:35.350 --> 01:11:36.750
A diamondless ring.
一枚没有钻石的戒指。

1746
01:11:37.010 --> 01:11:37.470
Yeah.
是的。

1747
01:11:37.730 --> 01:11:38.530
From his family.
来自他家族的。

1748
01:11:38.830 --> 01:11:40.830
He has a setting ready to go.
他已经准备好戒托了。

1749
01:11:41.110 --> 01:11:41.670
Exactly.
没错。

1750
01:11:42.990 --> 01:11:43.550
Jessica.
杰西卡。

1751
01:11:44.330 --> 01:11:45.270
We're sorry.
抱歉。

1752
01:11:45.750 --> 01:11:46.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1753
01:11:46.450 --> 01:11:46.790
Sorry.
抱歉。

1754
01:11:46.970 --> 01:11:47.810
He's off to Florida.
他要去佛罗里达了。

1755
01:11:48.170 --> 01:11:51.410
There was an alternate ending to this episode.
这一集原本有一个备选结局。

1756
01:11:51.790 --> 01:11:52.370
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

1757
01:11:52.550 --> 01:11:53.790
It's in the shooting draft.
就在拍摄剧本里。

1758
01:11:53.790 --> 01:11:55.310
It's a hilarious tag.
那是个非常搞笑的尾声。

1759
01:11:55.590 --> 01:11:57.530
I kind of felt like we should read it.
我觉得我们应该读一下。

1760
01:11:57.710 --> 01:11:58.410
Oh, okay.
哦，好的。

1761
01:11:58.410 --> 01:12:02.130
So, it's between Phyllis and Stanley.
所以，这是菲利斯和斯坦利之间的戏。

1762
01:12:02.490 --> 01:12:05.850
And, Jenna, you read Phyllis and I'll read Stanley.
珍娜，你读菲利斯的台词，我读斯坦利的。

1763
01:12:06.090 --> 01:12:06.430
Okay.
好的。

1764
01:12:07.470 --> 01:12:10.610
The script read, Interior Stanley's Desk Clump.
剧本上写着：内景，斯坦利的办公桌区。

1765
01:12:10.750 --> 01:12:11.130
Morning.
早上好。

1766
01:12:11.470 --> 01:12:14.810
Phyllis unplugs and takes Kathy's mouse from her desk.
菲利斯拔掉插头，从凯西的桌上拿走了她的鼠标。

1767
01:12:15.110 --> 01:12:16.530
Phyllis starts the scene.
菲利斯开始了这一幕。

1768
01:12:17.190 --> 01:12:18.530
I'll take this.
这个我拿走了。

1769
01:12:19.150 --> 01:12:20.530
Kathy's not here anymore.
凯西已经不在这儿了。

1770
01:12:20.790 --> 01:12:22.950
Phyllis looks at Stanley's desk.
菲利斯看向斯坦利的桌子。

1771
01:12:23.310 --> 01:12:24.570
What's with the stuff?
这些东西是怎么回事？

1772
01:12:24.570 --> 01:12:28.390
Well, I realize Florida isn't just a state, Phyllis.
嗯，我意识到佛罗里达不仅仅是一个州，菲利斯。

1773
01:12:28.530 --> 01:12:29.530
It's a state of mind.
它是一种心境。

1774
01:12:29.790 --> 01:12:30.790
Look at this.
看看这个。

1775
01:12:31.410 --> 01:12:33.190
Stanley points to a bottle of sand.
斯坦利指着一瓶沙子。

1776
01:12:33.770 --> 01:12:35.110
Is that cocaine?
那是可卡因吗？

1777
01:12:35.430 --> 01:12:36.630
It's my beach.
那是我的沙滩。

1778
01:12:37.150 --> 01:12:38.790
Stanley points to a bottle of water.
斯坦利指着一瓶水。

1779
01:12:39.270 --> 01:12:40.510
This is my ocean.
这是我的海洋。

1780
01:12:40.970 --> 01:12:44.010
Stanley picks up a flashlight and points it at his face.
斯坦利拿起手电筒，照向自己的脸。

1781
01:12:44.690 --> 01:12:45.590
Stanley continues.
斯坦利继续说道。

1782
01:12:45.950 --> 01:12:47.610
And this is my son.
而这是我的儿子。

1783
01:12:48.290 --> 01:12:51.190
Stanley spritzes some suntan lotion spray in the air.
斯坦利对着空气喷了一些防晒喷雾。

1784
01:12:51.190 --> 01:12:55.070
He sniffs the air, shuts his eyes, and starts softly moaning.
他嗅了嗅空气，闭上眼睛，开始轻声呻吟。

1785
01:12:55.290 --> 01:12:57.370
A small smile on his face.
脸上带着一丝微笑。

1786
01:12:58.550 --> 01:12:59.110
Stanley?
斯坦利？

1787
01:13:00.410 --> 01:13:00.970
Stanley?
斯坦利？

1788
01:13:01.430 --> 01:13:02.730
He doesn't respond.
他没有回应。

1789
01:13:03.490 --> 01:13:06.870
This would cut to a Stanley talking head where he would say,
接下来会切到斯坦利的单人采访，他会说：

1790
01:13:07.370 --> 01:13:11.330
Well, I just came back from paradise, which felt like a dream.
嗯，我刚从天堂回来，那感觉就像一场梦。

1791
01:13:11.510 --> 01:13:14.330
And now I feel like I woke up and I'm in hell.
而现在我觉得自己醒了，却身处地狱。

1792
01:13:14.610 --> 01:13:15.930
How the f*** are you?
你他妈过得怎么样？

1793
01:13:18.110 --> 01:13:19.370
End of episode.
剧集结束。

1794
01:13:19.370 --> 01:13:21.030
End of episode.
剧集结束。

1795
01:13:21.730 --> 01:13:25.070
Oh, thank you to Steve Burgess and Robert Padnick,
哦，感谢史蒂夫·伯吉斯和罗伯特·帕德尼克，

1796
01:13:25.210 --> 01:13:28.030
and also to Phil Shea for helping us fill out this episode.
也要感谢菲尔·谢伊帮我们完成了这一集的内容。

1797
01:13:28.210 --> 01:13:30.990
And thanks to you guys for sending in your questions and comments.
也感谢你们发来问题和评论。

1798
01:13:31.190 --> 01:13:32.170
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1799
01:13:32.330 --> 01:13:32.750
See you then.
到时候见。

1800
01:13:36.810 --> 01:13:38.790
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1801
